  "final_answer_preview": "Under the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, if you were forced at gunpoint to assist in a crime, the legal implications depend on the nature of the crime and the context of your involvement. Section 136 addresses assault or criminal force under grave provocation, which may provide a basis for a defense if you were coerced. However, if your actions fall under organized crime, Section 111(4) could impose severe penalties. The specific circumstances of coercion and your level of involvement would be critical in determining the outcome.",
